, "tool": "list_orders", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 42568, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Q2JeAAKZkzLdGKGQekfrbA", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 48305, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I placed part of the order, but not all of it, so I've stopped rather than risk a duplicate.\n\n**What happened:**\n- The first `place_order` call timed out. Retrying with the same idempotency key returned a partial-failure error, not a success.\n- `list_orders` shows **PO0001**, status `partially_placed`, shipping to HQ, from the primary vendor. It contains **3 \u00d7 DK-200 (new, $567)** only.\n- The **3 \u00d7 MN-27 monitors ($987) are not on any order.**\n\nI did not place a new order for the monitors, because you asked for a single purchase order and a separate one would break that. I also did not cancel PO0001, since that would refund and reverse a committed order.\n\n**Options for you to choose from:**\n1. **Order the monitors separately:** I place 3 \u00d7 MN-27 on a new PO to HQ from the primary vendor. Result: two POs, with the same total of $1,554.\n2. **Rebuild as one PO:** I cancel PO0001 (refund $567), then place one PO for 3 \u00d7 DK-200 and 3 \u00d7 MN-27 to HQ for $1,554. This meets the single-PO requirement but involves a cancel and a re-order.\n3. **Use the secondary vendor for the monitors:** I place 3 \u00d7 MN-27 through vendor B. This keeps PO0001 as is, but it is still two POs across two suppliers.\n\nAlso, PO0001 shows a shipping address of \"HQ\" exactly as you gave it. If HQ needs a specific street address or recipient name, please send it. The order total is under the $2,500 threshold, so manager approval isn't required for any of these options.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_011kumD2AatHtQdJ1iEfA9pN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"category": "dock"}, "name": "search_catalog", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_017EqZg45aDP38wkbSChZAdw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"category": "monitor"}, "name": "search_catalog", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "DK-200 is in stock as new equipment, so DK-210 isn't needed. The order totals $1,554 (3 \u00d7 $189 + 3 \u00d7 $329), which is under the $2,500 approval threshold. Placing the single order now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01ATqVCTLTyb8Xk9HB59BDjW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"lines": [{"sku": "DK-200", "qty": 3}, {"sku": "MN-27", "qty": 3}], "ship_to": "HQ", "idempotency_key": "new-hires-dk200-mn27-hq-3x3"}, "name": "place_order", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so I'm retrying with the same idempotency key. The service will return the original outcome rather than place a second order.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01SUWNd1jkttgwedg2HZtN1o", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"lines": [{"sku": "DK-200", "qty": 3}, {"sku": "MN-27", "qty": 3}], "ship_to": "HQ", "idempotency_key": "new-hires-dk200-mn27-hq-3x3"}, "name": "place_order", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The retry reports a partial failure: the first line item may have gone through and the order is incomplete. I'll check the order list before doing anything else so I don't duplicate anything.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Q2JeAAKZkzLdGKGQekfrbA", "caller": {"ty